10:26:43 AM | E2E Test Suite: Invoice Management Lifecycle > 2. Invoice Creation (POST /api/v1/invoices) > 2.1 Chauffeur creates a full invoice with auto-generated number and sender profile injection (POST /api/v1/invoices) | stdout

📝 USER STORY:
As a Chauffeur
I want to create an invoice for a completed job
So that I can bill my client with my business branding automatically applied

📋 BUSINESS RULES & PAYLOAD SPECIFICATIONS:
• Endpoint: POST /api/v1/invoices
• Authentication: Bearer JWT Token required
• 1. Invoice Details:
  - invoiceNumber: Auto-generated unique sequential identifier (e.g. "INV-000001")
  - invoiceAmount (number >= 0): Mandatory total amount to bill
  - issueDate (string | Date): Mandatory invoice issuance date
  - dueDateType ('on_receipt' | 'custom'): Mandatory due date type
  - customDueDate (string | Date): Required when dueDateType is 'custom'
  - currency (string): Defaults to 'USD'
• 2. Client Details (Mandatory Object):
  - clientName (string): Mandatory client/customer name
  - emailAddress (string): Mandatory client contact email
  - businessName (string): Optional client business/company name
  - phoneNumber (string): Optional client contact number
  - billingAddress (object): Mandatory { streetAddress, city, state, zipCode, country }
• 3. Message & Description Details:
  - description (string): Optional job / service description
  - messageToClient (string): Optional custom note or message to client
• 4. System Automation & Defaults:
  - status ('paid' | 'unpaid'): Defaults to 'unpaid'
  - senderDetails: Auto-injected from chauffeur's Invoice Profile if configured
  - Client Auto-Save: Automatically saves client to InvoiceClient directory upon invoice creation
• Response: toJSON transform formats _id → id and strips __v

